Dear Editors,

Please consider our manuscript entitled =E2=80=9CRegional medullary redox pro=
files in rats with atlantoaxial joint disorder=E2=80=9D for publication as an=
 Original Article in Physiological Research.

In this study, we examined redox-related biochemical changes in medullary tis=
sue encompassing the rostral ventrolateral medulla (RVLM) and adjacent region=
s in a rat model of atlantoaxial joint disorder. At 4 weeks post-surgery, mod=
el rats exhibited lower superoxide dismutase activity, higher malondialdehyde=
-related thiobarbituric acid (TBA) signals and higher NOX1/NOX4 protein signa=
ls than sham-operated controls. These findings provide additional regional bi=
ochemical evidence to complement the characterization of this cervical joint =
disorder model and may be of interest to researchers studying autonomic cardi=
ovascular regulation and redox biology.

Blood-pressure observations from the same experimental series were used in a =
related publication on Ang II/AT1 receptor signaling. That publication is cit=
ed, and its relationship to the present study is described in the manuscript.

This manuscript has not been published previously and is not under considerat=
ion for publication elsewhere. Supporting data and supplementary methods acco=
mpany the submission. Relevant ethics approval and disclosure statements are =
provided in the manuscript.

Thank you for your time and consideration.

